    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0225" n="215" xml:id="pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">892.248/46: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-17T11:00:00+07:00">July 17, 1941—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>350. My telegram No. 306, June 12, 5 p.m.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d225-f1"/> In
                    view of the enormous amount of unfavorable publicity in the Thai press over a
                    period of many months regarding the stopping of the war planes purchased by
                    Thailand, I recommend that the Department inform me by telegraph immediately
                    upon the settlement of the claim in order that favorable counteracting publicity
                    may be secured here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
